sub:assertion {
<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/wolfram2002-ch06-09> a <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/Claim>;
    dc:description "Changing one cell of the initial condition has characteristically different effects by class: in class 1 the change dies out, in class 2 it stays localized, in class 3 it spreads at a uniform rate to affect the whole system, and in class 4 it spreads only sporadically.";
    dc:type "computational-observation";
    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "The four classes respond differently to small changes in initial conditions";
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/context> "Stephen Wolfram, A New Kind of Science (Champaign, IL: Wolfram Media, 2002), Chapter 6, “Starting from Randomness”; section “Sensitivity to Initial Conditions” (from p. 250), p. 250. Scope: cellular automata of all four classes"
}
